0.03908772,-0.08311471,0.04061539,-0.02293978,-0.00631222,-0.05977168,0.14762254,-0.02266254,0.06065489,-0.03877699,-0.01285533,0.0952429,-0.06452481,0.02520652,0.02976101,0.01441891,0.0357612,-0.01506425,-0.02236747,-0.05440668,0.02099518,0.03260207,0.02276408,0.05396168,-0.05915762,-0.01414974,-0.03202236,-0.04595215,-0.02339675,-0.01967026,-0.0570135,0.01865908,0.02101317,-0.00531228,0.0974803,0.02306387,0.01326604,-0.04360627,0.0012706,-0.03468537,0.01496087,-0.07433622,-0.00353325,-0.07495406,-0.01349845,-0.01888827,0.01431725,-0.01621743,-0.03873143,0.04482721,-0.03675819,0.06426627,0.06540781,-0.00127918,0.00443982,-0.0950761,0.07370061,-0.04215926,-0.00021425,0.03182837,-0.00615309,-0.01708007,0.01806602,-0.00978794,-0.00281548,-0.04859967,-0.1902466,-0.03759467,-0.01932118,-0.05084854,0.12703864,-0.05386159,0.00578944,-0.01872886,0.0082656,0.0852855,0.04217302,0.03098139,-0.04370315,-0.03368316,-0.02073163,-0.02449606,0.02035881,0.01918459,-0.06719963,0.04079112,-0.03583034,0.04871919,-0.05845401,-0.09480023,0.00807841,-0.09582011,0.17078315,0.04955009,0.10382684,0.10517401,0.01833798,-0.0049394,0.02918552,-0.18033673,0.05678001,0.0636077,0.01587391,-0.03429393,0.04771834,-0.05645965,0.04048843,-0.02014931,-0.03001149,-0.0540945,-0.06214581,-0.01221347,0.00167683,-0.02571426,0.02197368,-0.02857352,-0.00104288,-0.01954914,-0.01835204,0.03503089,-0.05913746,0.02026473,-0.06792177,-0.04689502,-0.02433448,0.0810702,0.00629233,0.00743358,0.01159659,-0.01748024,0.0174692,-0.00718194,0.01024603,0.00647114,0.01401931,-0.00860625,0.04714412,0.16889761,-0.02657461,0.00552781,0.01315875,0.02145224,0.08259235,0.00371676,0.04419579,0.01390938,0.02285658,-0.03877542,0.00683459,0.03556603,0.06858741,-0.01714154,0.00915017,-0.07179638,0.02068211,0.01161249,-0.01359127,0.02490226,-0.07089721,-0.0352955,-0.0018445,0.01158301,-0.21777113,0.04697007,-0.02828803,0.04590543,-0.05773661,0.03090484,0.02674892,-0.03658176,-0.07646719,-0.04033399,-0.03870422,-0.00415266,0.05663058,-0.0391452,-0.00994629,-0.04027072,0.11609064,-0.03416805,0.05391173,-0.00397621,-0.00779349,0.04549477,0.18463998,-0.05386482,-0.01100602,-0.01989615,0.03288021,0.02260987,-0.00974326,0.01614149,0.01565438,0.00713625,0.06219393,-0.02986137,-0.00131124,0.04236867,-0.03318365,0.00002528,0.0520552,-0.02052236,-0.0220438,0.02141586,-0.03452111,-0.01385758,0.08350028,0.03744541,-0.03579673,-0.04902121,-0.01230374,0.0149139,0.05326499,0.03739926,0.03096033,0.00225222,0.04088703,0.02288904,-0.01165668,-0.03671253,-0.02127292,-0.03935604,0.00231251,-0.07268266,0.01871431,0.04553539,0.01957246],"last_embed":{"tokens":433,"hash":"h4yqa2"}}},"text":null,"length":0,"last_read":{"hash":"h4yqa2","at":1778905921187},"key":"Clippings/Soviet Psychology Dialectics as Logic.md###5: Hegel – Dialectics as Logic","lines":[18,250],"size":72624,"outlinks":[{"title":"*Shorter Logic*","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/slintro.htm#SL2","line":13},{"title":"***shows forth God as he is in his eternal essence before the creation of Nature and of a Finite Spirit***","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/hl/hlintro.htm#HL1_50","line":23},{"title":"A comparison of the forms to which Spirit has risen in the worlds of Practice and Religion, and of Science in every department of knowledge Positive and Speculative - a comparison of these with the form which Logic, that is, Spirit’s knowledge of its own pure essence - has attained, shows such a glaring discrepancy that it cannot fail to strike the most superficial observer that the latter is inadequate to the lofty development of the former, and unworthy of it.","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/hl/hlintro.htm#HL1_51a","line":37},{"title":"such logic had no other business than could be done through the activity of simple formal thought, and so it certainly produced nothing that one could not otherwise have done just as well","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/hl/hlintro.htm#HL1_58","line":47},{"title":"Lenin’s translation and materialist interpretation","target":"https://www.marxists.org/archive/lenin/works/1914/cons-logic/preface.htm#LCW38_92d1","line":71},{"title":"In all human contemplation there is thought, just as thought is the general in all conceptions, recollections, and on the whole any mental activity, in all wishes, desires, etc. All these are only further specifications of thought. While we so conceive thought, it itself appears in another aspect than when we only speak; we have intellectual power over and above any other abilities, like contemplation, imagination, will and the like.","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/sl_ii.htm#SL21","line":73},{"title":"effects everything human and makes humanity human","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/slintro.htm#SL2_2","line":75},{"title":"***appears*** at first not in the form of thought but as feeling, intuition, imagination - ***forms*** that are to be distinguished from thought as form","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/slintro.htm#SL2_3","line":77},{"title":"***determination*** of sensation, intuition, images, ideas, aims, obligations, etc., and also thoughts and concepts","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/slintro.htm#SL3","line":77},{"title":"the nature of thought is itself dialectics, that as understanding it must fall into the negative of itself, into contradiction...","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/slintro.htm#SL11_1","line":99},{"title":"thought, despairing of managing ***by itself*** to resolve the contradiction into which it had got itself, turns back to the solutions and reliefs that were the spirit’s lot in its other modes and forms","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/slintro.htm#SL11_1","line":103},{"title":"these three aspects in no case constitute three ***parts*** of logic, but are only ***moments of any logically real nature***, that is of any concept or of any truth in general","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/sl_vi.htm#SL79","line":119},{"title":"Thought as ***understanding*** remains stuck in firm determination and does not get beyond differentiation of the latter; such a limited abstraction applies to it as existing and being for itself.","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/sl_vi.htm#SL80","line":125},{"title":"The ***dialectical*** moment is the own self-abolition of such ultimate determinations and their transition into their opposites.","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/sl_vi.htm#SL80","line":127},{"title":"The ***speculative or positively reasonable*** conceives the unity of determinations in their opposition, the ***affirmation*** that is contained in their resolution and their transition","target":"https://www.marxists.org/reference/archive/hegel/works/sl/sl_divis.htm#SL82","line":129}],"class_name":"SmartBlock"},
